I like the idea of having the superhero characters, but I have a few suggestions:

1)  Don't let the user elect to become a superhero (like selecting a Wizard)
	let the game decide.  For example--in the begining of the game I
	choose "Barbarian".  Nethack has a small probablity of generating
	Conan.  If it does it gives the message "You feel special" or something 
	and the game proceeds as normal, but a special level is generated.  
	When the potential Conan reaches this level he must face some task
	to get a "huge ornate sword". When this is wielded Conan comes
	to life..."You feel incredibly strong", "You feel very sturdy", etc ...

2)  Eventually The superhero must face his archenemy on another special level.

3)  There is no reason to limit this to heros, what's wrong with villians?

4)  Don't just limit it to comic books.  I'd like to see Perseus do battle
	with Medusa.

  Superheroes wern't usually born that way, but come into existance through 
some trumatic event (I don't know how I'd code the death of Bruce Wayne's 
parents though).  I think this change would make it more "realistic".  Plus
the rarity of the superhero makes the game more interesting (like finding
your first WoW!).

    Just some ideas.

	Chris


